ref 17592186550520} {:answer/id #uuid "702d8457-7a04-5f81-b354-457a65777dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550650} {:answer/id #uuid "9ebfa448-95fd-50cb-8944-07f3949c13df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550774} {:answer/id #uuid "a181d0c5-2f8c-57a8-860d-c4b8dd85032a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 19 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 14 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ -9 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ -11 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550784} {:answer/id #uuid "bd434e23-296a-58e6-8c06-72a49aab1760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 19 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 14 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ -9 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ -11 & 4 & {4}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550774} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c23c67-d5f0-5435-9ff0-f58fa6b0cfc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551214}] :question/id #uuid "1dfba625-81c0-581d-a463-4b6d422c9f73" :question/math-academy-id "q-139660" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $19$ | $14$ | $-9$ | $-11$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $19$ | $14$ | $-9$ | $-11$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 19 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Design Matrix When the Regression Curve Contains Zero Coefficients"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133807 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133616 :question/id #uuid "f5354fe5-fa4b-5443-a097-40174b0b7b16" :question/math-academy-id "e-5613" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $2$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression (in terms of $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$) for the vector of coefficients $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ of the curve $y=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3$ that best fits the data. \n\n![](images/17/172f8147d4d58d4d3edc42f96e3fb248f59cb749ed0e387c9c8bcddfec08bf79.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}}$ to the system \n\n$$\nX \\boldsymbol{\\beta} = \\mathbf{y},\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by $X^T,$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\nX^T \\! X {\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}} = X^T \\mathbf{y}.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X^T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}} = (X^T \\! X )^{-1} X^T \\mathbf{y}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0f92926-0c15-554a-8fba-55b05d435980" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5d8fcea-b4b8-5ab9-8557-698be9f94434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(XX^{T})^{-1}Xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130799} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6cbb18-0b93-5e6e-a3e1-3d5468f5ecf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X^{T}(XX^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130800} {:answer/id #uuid "17b8b33f-3067-5d03-b8a0-a88f09a7ac9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130801} {:answer/id #uuid "1ed0b824-20e8-5962-b3ad-71fe98e946e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X(X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130802} {:answer/id #uuid "735ef892-f539-5a92-9bd8-09d02a2900bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X(X^{T}X)^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130803}] :answer-field/id #uuid "41d2744c-3c33-50c8-af80-dc263247fec4" :answer-field/key "se